# Lock-screen information: divert module 31's painter hold-icon tail
# call to the lock-screen routine inside the module 31 segment
# extension payload (composition: work/mod31_compose/
# mod31_compose.md). This scratch copy regenerates the branch target
# for the routine's composed position: payload offset 6760, exec
# 0x030808B0 (the standalone scratch link base was 0x0307EE48, the
# first byte past module 31's stock code segment; the routine moved
# because the payload leads with the M3U trampoline and the
# bridge+parser blob). Design: work/ui_features/ui_features.md;
# renderer contract and the build-ready specification:
# work/ui_features/renderer/renderer.md; build evidence:
# work/ui_features/lockscreen_build/lockscreen_build.md.
name: ui-lockscreen-title
kind: module
module: 31
region: code
address: 0x0307e89e
gate: build refuses unless the 4 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass the grown-build validator.
  Do NOT stack without the module 31 segment extension build
  (--grow 31:code: with the generated payload.bin) carrying
  the lock-screen blob at the branch target. If the payload layout
  moves the routine again, regenerate the branch bytes from
  the composition build with the new base (it emits site33.bin);
  the routine is position-dependent only on its
  link base.
expect: e4f72fbf
replace: 02f007b8
rationale: The site is the last instruction of the module 31 painter's
  flag-0x2E segment: flag test-cleared, the byte at 0x030230ec loaded,
  {r4, lr} popped, r0 = 0x26 + bit 2 of that byte, and the stock bytes
  are the tail call B.W DrawImage (0x03063700). The patch redirects
  that one branch to the lock-screen routine, which performs the
  displaced DrawImage call first with r0 unchanged, then, only when
  SAVEINFO +0x60 == 1, draws the track title from the UTF-16 name
  buffer 0x030235ce through the stock text routine 0x03062cee under
  the display-mode bracket 0x0306316e and Display's pen colours, plus a
  separately gated elapsed/total line from the pinned file-info
  position fields. With +0x60 != 1 the patched firmware is
  behaviour-identical to stock at this site: one DrawImage call, no
  other observable state touched.
